Client & Franchise Outcomes — Enterprise Container Modernisation and Developer Enablement
Led enterprise container modernisation to accelerate adoption of approved RHEL 9 UBI Minimal/Micro images and significantly improve the quality, security and maintainability of Citi’s container ecosystem. Partnered closely with Middleware Engineering across 14+ image families and 100+ distinct image variations to accelerate the delivery of approved runtime images, resolve certificate, keystore and image-family compatibility issues, and enable application teams to adopt updated RHEL base images more quickly.
Drove a sustainable shift in engineering practices, with the vast majority of intermediate image variations onboarded to Renovate, reduced image footprints, removal of unnecessary libraries and credentials, and more timely image refreshes as updated base images became available. Advanced runtime optimisation through leaner Java runtimes using jlink and removal of unnecessary components, including AppDynamics and NGC where applicable. Promoted multi-stage builds, automated base-image updates, regular repaving and Citi’s container engineering standards, supported by DiP adoption across 200+ team repositories and developer education materials.
Delivered measurable improvements across the container estate: RHEL 9 images adoption increased from 3.4% in March to 14.8%, while RHEL 7 images decreased to less than 400 only. Average container image age fell from 185 to 98 days, a reduction of approximately 47%. Image optimisation delivered approximately 110 MB of size reduction across around 80% of assessed images, alongside average reductions of more than 60% in Critical CVEs and 70% in High CVEs.
This work has delivered both a technical and cultural shift in how Citi’s engineering teams build, maintain and consume container images. As recognised in my manager’s mid-year feedback, the improvements have had a significant impact across the developer enterprise, strengthening security posture while reducing recurring vulnerability remediation effort and improving engineering efficiency.

